## Six review domains

### Content

The new surface is free technical Laboratory configuration/inspection, not a new assessed course module. Boundary copy consistently says no real Azure provisioning, public address, NAT, VM runtime, packets, flow state or verified application connectivity. Standard/Regional/Static IPv4 Public IP is a configuration resource created with the Firewall and stores `address:null`. The private allocator is explicitly synthetic. Policy→RCG→Network Collection→Rule, collection action, group-before-collection priority and first terminating match agree with the retained [processing](../reviews/evidence/pr67/sources/processing.txt) and [policy](../reviews/evidence/pr67/sources/policy.txt) bodies and the official hierarchy image.

I verified all13 saved HTML hashes/lengths/date metadata and both official reference image hashes, then inspected the source passages rather than relying on the extracts file. FAQ directly supports same Firewall/VNet RG, same Firewall/VNet/PublicIP subscription, dedicated minimum/26 and no subnet NSG. The50-character FAQ versus80-character general naming-table discrepancy is disclosed as a conservative subset. Same-region/same-subscription Policy, no Firewall-subnet UDR, per-parent priority uniqueness and custom-only groups are simulator bounds, not universal Azure restrictions. Actual standard Firewall ARM example pairs Standard/Regional/Static IPv4. The source provides stateful established TCP/UDP responses even with reverse-new-initiation Deny. No reverse Allow rule is invented. Source-capture dating remains limited as PR67-FINAL-02 describes.

### Technical

I read all five v35 files, the engine/server adapters, SQL006, shared form/inventory/routing/inspection changes, and unchanged repository transaction logic. The projection restores actual appliance route identity/IP after frozen LPM/source selection; no placeholder None route is persisted. Forward and return next-hop lookups, hub onward/return routes and actual endpoint VNet IDs all constrain positive inspection. Receiving Data→Hub and App→Hub flags are checked in the correct directions; hub outgoing flags cannot substitute. NSG evaluation reuses the three-valued matcher and preserves unknown/default-tag behavior. Forward outbound/inbound layers can deny despite Firewall Allow. The model does not evaluate reverse new-initiation rules as established-response policy.

Read-only analysis preserves World/events, binds workspace/model/revision and retains not-sent/not-verified semantics. Actual PostgreSQL tests passed for atomic Firewall/PublicIP rollback, competing writers, lost-response idempotency, request-identity conflict, through/reset replay, immutable events, separate sessions, wrong workspace, unauthenticated read, corrupt-history503 and cold/populated/repeated006 setup. SQL001–005 and repository.ts remain unchanged. PR67-FINAL-01 is nevertheless a major client configuration-truth defect and blocks acceptance of this stamp.

